kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-k4"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-k4"],"id":"long.record-257bm-k4","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.131 (The returning endpoint need not be larger)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.131, p. 80, label record:257bm-k4","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Theorem 6.78 is unconditional, but its witness is $\\exists c\\le n$, not $\\exists c$ large: $2c-2$ may be $\\le n$, so the endpoint need not grow. The countermodel of Theorem 6.127 is the explicit falsifier of the naive hope that growth comes for free: $\\mathrm{boundedDoubleOrRecycleModel}(n):=(n=6)$ satisfies the same transition schema plus a seed and is not cofinal. Growth is recovered only inside $\\mathrm{ProtectedExactLocalMersenneRow}$ (Theorem 6.71), whose invariants $\\mathrm{endpoint}<2\\cdot\\mathrm{cutoff}$ and $\\mathrm{new\\_above\\_cutoff}$ force $c>\\mathrm{cutoff}$ hence $2c-2>\\mathrm{endpoint}$ ; and maintaining those invariants is precisely what needs the strict-upper (sharp capacity) fill of Theorem 6.75 rather than this general recycling theorem.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257bm-k4","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257bm-k4","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-k4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exists_seeded_bounded_double_or_recycle_model%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-k4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exists_seeded_bounded_double_or_recycle_model%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","